<title>BRAZIL: Brazil agency ok's Colgate Anakol purchase.</title>
<headline>Brazil agency ok's Colgate Anakol purchase.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's Administrative Economic Defense Council (CADE), a government antitrust body, has ruled in favour of a $1.04 billion buyout of an oral-hygiene products company by Colgate-Palmolive, a government official said.</p>
<p>He said Tuesday's approval by the antitrust body of Colgate-Palmolive's purchase of Anakol, manufacturer of the Kolynos brand of toothpaste, gives the U.S. firm a 79-percent share of the Brazilian toothpaste market.</p>
</text>
